+{"title":"Prompt calibration: what the record misses","icon":"🎯","description":"Four of your voice prompts, refined by Haiku and Sonnet: the asks and questions no task holds yet.","class":"/live/LivePage.js"}
+{"content":{"add":{"id":"dlkgoxa6","type":"part-text","text":"Four of your voice prompts from the 11-06 cloud session were checked against the 24 tasks on the voice app's record. **Sonnet did it better and cheaper than Haiku** (about $0.03 a prompt). Below is what no task holds yet. Nothing here has been filed: each card is a suggestion. Full results: [calibration/results.md](/framework/ai/sessions/2026/11/06/spawned/mastermind-session-truth/calibration/results.md)."}},"by":"mastermind-session-truth","ts":"2026-11-07T06:28:45.793Z"}
+{"content":{"add":{"id":"fix-the-page-error-after-reload","type":"part-card","title":"🐛 Fix the page error after reload","text":"**Suggested task** (#114, \"your agents broke my page\"). After \"page out of date, reload\", the page threw a JavaScript error (\"P is not a function\"). The rule half (worktree, smoke test, merge only when ready) is already in agents.md. The error itself has no task."}},"by":"mastermind-session-truth","ts":"2026-11-07T06:28:47.586Z"}
+{"content":{"add":{"id":"page-storage-and-loading-at-scale","type":"part-card","title":"📄 Page storage and loading at scale","text":"**Suggested task** (#95). Converge pages on one storage system: embedded first, then a sub-page with its own folder past a threshold. Study how loading scales.\n\n**Question:** when a parent page loads, does it load and replay every child page and delta?\n\n**Suggested task:** a page index (`index.jsonl` with icon, title and preview) loaded one level deep. You said you had asked before, so past work should be searched first."}},"by":"mastermind-session-truth","ts":"2026-11-07T06:28:49.871Z"}
+{"content":{"add":{"id":"page-settings-with-a-files-tab","type":"part-card","title":"⚙️ Page settings with a Files tab","text":"**Suggested task** (#116). Any page gets a settings screen. Its Files tab lists the page's folders and files and opens a file with syntax highlighting.\n\n**Suggested task:** breadcrumbs exactly mirror `window.location.pathname`.\n\n**Note, not a task:** you said not to build the toolbar and debug ideas yet."}},"by":"mastermind-session-truth","ts":"2026-11-07T06:28:51.774Z"}
+{"content":{"add":{"id":"plan-first-and-say-who-else-is-editing","type":"part-card","title":"🧠 Plan first, and say who else is editing","text":"**Suggested task** (#116). A plan is the simplified class architecture. It is amended as decisions change, and then the build goes ahead without waiting for approval. (Close to the Plan idea in core/Task, written down but not built.)\n\n**Suggested task:** the live-page docs warn that several agents may edit at once, so never assume the state is what you last saw.\n\n**Question:** can the item tool read one property (`page.content`)? It can now: `item({path, read: \"content\"})`."}},"by":"mastermind-session-truth","ts":"2026-11-07T06:28:54.476Z"}
+{"content":{"add":{"id":"already-held-by-a-task","type":"part-card","title":"✅ Already held by a task","text":"#27 (\"why we haven't been completing our sessions\") is fully covered by close-with-proof and past-work-audit. Both models agreed."}},"by":"mastermind-session-truth","ts":"2026-11-07T06:28:55.524Z"}
